  "homeFeedingTrendInfoTitle": "How this tracker works",
  "homeFeedingTrendInfoBody": "We use the last 14 days of feeds as a reference (bottle and breast; solids aren’t included). At least 2 days with feeds are needed before we leave “learning” and can compare.\n\nAt this time of day, we compare today’s total so far with the usual range from those days: below usual, as usual, or above usual.\n\n“Usually still takes” is an estimate: the median of what they typically reach by end of day, minus what they’ve already taken today.\n\nBreastfeeding can’t be measured in ml like a bottle, so we turn nursing minutes into an approximate equivalent. These figures are a guide, not exact measurements. If anything seems off, check with your pediatrician.",
